        {
          "id": "dc779938-4e75-3359-ac6f-abda9e015fcf",
          "content": {
            "id": "dc779938-4e75-3359-ac6f-abda9e015fcf",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Berkshire Hathaway preps CEO change, Cracker Barrel dumps ad firm",
            "description": "<p>Yahoo Finance's <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/john-hyland/\">John Hyland</a> tracks today's top moving stocks and biggest market stories in this<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-minute/\"> Market Minute</a>.</p>\n<p>Warren Buffett's Berkshire Hathaway (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BRK-B\">BRK-B</a>, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BRK-A\">BRK-A</a>) voted to separate its chairman and CEO roles, allowing Greg Abel to succeed Buffett as CEO next year.</p>\n<p>Applied Materials (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AMAT\">AMAT</a>) stock is under pressure after the company noted it expects to incur a $600 million loss from Chinese sales restrictions.</p>\n<p>Cracker Barrel (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/CBRL\">CBRL</a>) has officially ended its professional relationship with the marketing firm behind its controversial and brief logo change.</p>\n<p>Stay up to date on the latest market action, minute-by-minute, with <a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-minute/\">Yahoo Finance's Market Minute.</a></p>",
            "summary": "Yahoo Finance's John Hyland tracks today's top moving stocks and biggest market stories in this Market Minute. Warren Buffett's Berkshire Hathaway (BRK-B, BRK-A) voted to separate its chairman and CEO roles, allowing Greg Abel to succeed Buffett as CEO next year. Applied Materials (AMAT) stock is under pressure after the company noted it expects to incur a $600 million loss from Chinese sales restrictions. Cracker Barrel (CBRL) has officially ended its professional relationship with the marketing firm behind its controversial and brief logo change. Stay up to date on the latest market action, minute-by-minute, with Yahoo Finance's Market Minute.",
